From 83d9e7133e3e0db75152bf74bac4ed95adfe638d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:16:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] Pin the Claude CLI by bytes (compromise C2) and record
 the version per call (gap rank 16, chaos D4)

- src/cli-pin.mjs resolveCli(): with a lock named (FOUNDRY_CLI_LOCK), the verified binary at
  .foundry/cli/<sha256>/claude by absolute path, hashed once per process and re-hashed when
  its identity (dev, inode, size, mtime, ctime) changes; CLI_DRIFT on other bytes,
  CLI_UNPINNED when the pin is not acquired; never a fallback to PATH. cliPinChange()
  for resume comparisons.
- claude-cli provider: pinned calls run the pinned path (engineVersion names its sha256);
  unpinned calls ask --version on every call (about 50 ms; it was cached per binary per
  process, so a CLI that updated mid-run was misrecorded). A pin that cannot be honoured
  fails as MODEL_PROTOCOL naming the CLI_ code.
- verify-run warns MIXED_ENGINE_VERSIONS when one harness served a run in two versions.
- DISABLE_UPDATES joins CHILD_ENV_ALLOWED; policy 2026-10-21.3 sets DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER and
  DISABLE_UPDATES for claude -p children; executor sessions always get both. runClaudeCode
  runs the pinned CLI (kept read-only in the sandbox) when a lock is named.
- research/manifests/claude-cli.lock.json: 2.1.306 sha256/size per platform from the
  release manifest (HTTPS; the installed CLI matches linux-x64), npm sha512 as a second
  root; signature NOT verified (the keyserver key has no user ID; recorded as such).
- scripts/fetch-cli.mjs: fetch or copy the raw binary, verify, never npm install; 1 GB
  disk guard; GC keeps 2 versions, never the lock's or one an unfinished run references.
Tests: tests/cli-pin.test.mjs 5/5 (fake CLIs; one check hashes the installed CLI), and
the env/version pins in models-port, claude-cli-env and executor-sandbox.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011geBy7JvDqKuqhDyfmzd1U
